WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.840 --> 00:01:06.960
[Drumming]

00:01:11.666 --> 00:01:18.432
[Narrator:] On the great western bulge of Africa is Liberia, Africa's only Republic.

00:01:18.433 --> 00:01:24.233
During the past quarter-century, Liberia's importance as a rubber-producing nation

00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:29.433
has gained for her stature and recognition throughout the world.

00:01:29.433 --> 00:01:34.566
In Liberia today are millions upon millions of rubber trees,

00:01:34.566 --> 00:01:42.206
the majority of which produce more latex than any other trees anywhere.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:47.233
To operate the immense plantations on which these trees are grown

00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:52.813
requires the combined skills and labor of tens of thousands of workers,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:59.860
the health and well-being of whom are vitally essential to the welfare of the nation as a whole.

00:01:59.866 --> 00:02:07.986
Safeguarding the health of their rubber workers is both an economic necessity and a moral obligation.

00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:15.733
In a very real sense, the development of research in, and practice of,

00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:21.413
tropical medicine in Liberia is a by-product of her ever-expanding rubber industry.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:32.660
As rubber is vital to Liberia's economy, so is an adequate medical program essential to her progress and prosperity.

00:02:33.733 --> 00:02:42.999
In order to understand the nature of the medical program that is today underway in Liberia, one must first examine the country itself.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:52.700
Located barely above the equator, on the edge of the vast rainforest of Equatorial Africa, Liberia's climate is humid and generally warm.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:03:00.620
The rainfall is heavy, between 90 and 160 inches each year.

00:03:10.466 --> 00:03:15.599
The abundant streams and rivers resulting from this heavy rainfall keep the numerous valleys

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:22.800
fertile and verdant and provide favorable conditions for the growing of almost any crop.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:29.833
Even the three or four month dry season fails seriously to retire Liberia's abundant agriculture.

00:03:29.833 --> 00:03:36.999
For even then, there are usually enough showers and light rains to maintain favorable growth.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:46.866
With a climate so ideally suited to agriculture, 
it is not surprising to find Liberians an agrarian people living close to the land and engaged in

00:03:46.866 --> 00:03:52.532
pursuits that are intimately related to the necessities of everyday living.

00:03:52.533 --> 00:03:57.966
Most Liberians are tribespeople who work and live very simply.

00:03:57.966 --> 00:04:03.566
Their daily activities are devoted largely to taking care of their immediate needs.

00:04:03.566 --> 00:04:12.666
In these respects they are typical of native inhabitants of many tropical climates.

00:04:22.633 --> 00:04:31.233
Agriculture is inherently easy because of the soil's fertility and the fact that crops are not severely restricted to seasons.

00:04:31.233 --> 00:04:41.199
Even on casual inspection of the landscape, it is evident that here almost anything will grow.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:48.133
On the one hand, this lush productivity resulting from the climate and rainfall is a blessing.

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:51.366
On the other, it is a threat.

00:04:51.366 --> 00:04:53.599
A menace and a liability.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:59.720
For the same conditions that make for an abundance of vegetables, forest products, and flowers are also favorable

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:07.920
to the growth and development of the micro-organisms that cause ruinous diseases.

00:05:17.633 --> 00:05:24.099
For example, while some of Liberia's streams are pure, others play a grim role as carriers

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:29.433
of malicious dysenteries and many other waterborne diseases.

00:05:29.433 --> 00:05:39.033
To help prevent these and to reduce the continuous hazard of malaria, Liberia's sanitation program today calls for almost incessant spraying

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:44.293
of surface streams and the land around them.

00:05:47.566 --> 00:05:52.932
Before the advent of the Firestone Rubber Plantations, swamplands and stagnant pools

00:05:52.933 --> 00:05:59.633
provided ideal breeding places for anopheline mosquitos, the carriers of malaria.

00:05:59.633 --> 00:06:05.499
Today with a broad medical and sanitation program in progress, this stagnant water is methodically

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:11.133
drained to prevent the formation of larvae breeding pools.

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:21.233
Foliage and trees along rivers and streams are cleared in order to fight trypanosomiasis or African sleeping sickness, at its source.

00:06:21.233 --> 00:06:27.533
This kind of growth provides shelter and breeding areas for the tsetse or glossina flies,

00:06:27.533 --> 00:06:33.566
several species of which are the carriers of this baffling and frequently fatal disease.

00:06:33.566 --> 00:06:43.386
Agricultural projects, such as the growing of rubber trees, also aid in the elimination of the tsetse fly breeding areas.

00:06:54.233 --> 00:07:04.533
Today in heavily populated plantation areas, water is impounded, filtered, and chlorinated to make it usable for cooking and drinking.

00:07:04.533 --> 00:07:08.773
Preventive measures like these are doubly important on the rubber plantations

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:14.000
because of the congestion that accompanies both working and living.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:20.833
On the plantations, thousands work together in close proximity.

00:07:20.833 --> 00:07:25.399
In the interior, many native villagers are frequently overcrowded.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:31.960
Once it takes hold, almost any disease becomes a potential epidemic.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:40.433
It is with this realization that sanitary preventive measures, like the daily inspection of latrines,

00:07:40.433 --> 00:07:46.199
have been instituted on the plantations and are rigorously enforced.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:51.066
But by far the most effective preventive factor is immunization.

00:07:51.066 --> 00:07:57.799
For example, twice yearly the resident population of the Firestone Plantations, numbering about 40,000,

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:03.566
is vaccinated against smallpox, which is endemic to much of Liberia.

00:08:03.566 --> 00:08:09.466
Each native village has at least one dresser station, staffed by trained medical orderlies

00:08:09.466 --> 00:08:16.932
who administer first-aid, care for minor ailments, and make simple diagnoses.

00:08:16.933 --> 00:08:21.233
The orderlies also make mass surveys of diseases.

00:08:21.233 --> 00:08:27.333
Here they are making preliminary tests for African trypanosomiasis, or sleeping sickness,

00:08:27.333 --> 00:08:33.066
by examining the cervical glands in the back of the neck.

00:08:33.066 --> 00:08:38.432
Unless acutely ill, tribespeople rarely seek medical aid.

00:08:38.433 --> 00:08:43.033
An unbalanced diet accustoms them to fatigue and low metabolism,

00:08:43.033 --> 00:08:48.113
and few are able even to recognize the presence of early symptoms of disease.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:54.760
This plantation worker complaining of an acute abdominal pain which he has suffered for four days,

00:08:54.766 --> 00:09:01.666
has come to his local dresser station only because the pain is intense.

00:09:01.666 --> 00:09:06.046
The orderlies, unable to diagnose the case adequately, send him to the

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:13.360
plantation base hospital for further examination by an American doctor.

00:09:13.366 --> 00:09:18.386
Once daily, or more frequently if necessary, a hospital bus whose route

00:09:18.386 --> 00:09:28.140
covers all plantation dresser stations transports such patients to the base hospital.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:34.380
To the hospital come many abdominal cases.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:40.533
Physical illnesses such as hernias, sprains,  bruises, and fractures are common.

00:09:40.533 --> 00:09:46.913
Partially, this results from an unbalanced diet, which is frequently deficient in proteins.

00:10:38.133 --> 00:10:45.833
[Narrator:] Patients referred to the hospital by the local station orderlies are examined first in the outpatient department of the hospital.

00:10:45.833 --> 00:10:52.233
The native medical personnel on the Firestone Plantations are about one hundred in number.

00:10:52.233 --> 00:11:06.633
All of them have been trained by American doctors and nurses who direct the hospital staff.

00:11:33.866 --> 00:11:39.632
In the outpatient department, a competent American doctor examines the abdominal case

00:11:39.633 --> 00:11:44.413
and diagnoses it tentatively as amebic abscess of the liver.

00:11:54.733 --> 00:12:02.466
After diagnosis, the doctor orders the patient admitted to the hospital for surgical treatment.

00:12:02.466 --> 00:12:08.832
In the early part of the medical program, natives were dubious of what they termed foreign doctors.

00:12:08.833 --> 00:12:17.993
But their doubts and fears were dispelled as a result of cures effected and the obvious efficiency of modern medical techniques and equipment.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:33.860
From the outpatient department, the abdominal case is admitted to the surgical ward in this base hospital.

00:12:53.966 --> 00:13:05.086
First, blood samples are taken, from which blood counts and blood tests will be made.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:21.866
The blood tests themselves are made in the hospital laboratory by skilled native technicians.

00:13:21.866 --> 00:13:28.506
The laboratory facilities in the Firestone Hospital in Liberia are completely modern in all respects.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:55.233
An x-ray examination is made to confirm the preliminary diagnosis.

00:13:55.233 --> 00:14:01.366
The pattern of common diseases is such that the preliminary diagnosis is generally accurate,

00:14:01.366 --> 00:14:07.006
but there have been instances where x-rays have altered the early diagnostic examination.

00:14:11.466 --> 00:14:16.266
In this case of abscess of the liver, surgery was considered advisable.

00:14:18.733 --> 00:14:27.999
Equipment, sterilization, and medical skills attendant upon surgery in the Firestone Hospital 
compare favorably with those existing anywhere.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:36.180
The extremely high percentage of successful surgery attests to the validity of modern medical techniques in primitive surroundings.

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:45.566
Amoebiasis, here undergoing operative treatment, is highly prevalent in most tropical countries.

00:14:45.566 --> 00:14:49.866
A waterborne disease, it is a development of chronic amoebic dysentery.

00:14:49.866 --> 00:14:54.432
The surgical objective is that of draining the hepatic abscesses.

00:14:54.433 --> 00:15:03.673
Amoebiasis affect an average of 40 to 50 percent
of the entire native population because of polluted water.

00:15:10.533 --> 00:15:15.066
The phrase "tropical medicine" indicates cosmopolitan medicine.

00:15:15.066 --> 00:15:25.066
It comprises the great majority of diseases common to the temperate climate, and in addition, a relative few which are peculiar to the tropics.

00:15:25.066 --> 00:15:31.399
The deep tropics are the most abundant of all pathological laboratories.

00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:39.366
After surgery the patient is removed to the convalescent ward, where the care he receives differs little from that offered in hospitals

00:15:39.366 --> 00:15:46.666
in Des Moines, Hartford, Tucson, Portland, New Orleans, or San Diego.

00:15:49.066 --> 00:15:55.866
The plantation hospital is staffed by American doctors and nurses and is supplement ed by native personnel,

00:15:55.866 --> 00:16:02.232
most of whom have learned readily and function devotedly at a highly competent level.

00:16:02.233 --> 00:16:13.466
The cases most frequently encountered in the general wards are malarias, schistosomiasis, carried by water snails, yaws, hernias, goiters,

00:16:13.466 --> 00:16:24.086
intestinal worms, dysenteries, filariases, traumatic injuries, and pulmonary, bone and skin diseases.

00:16:31.533 --> 00:16:35.833
In pleasant, easy surroundings the patient recovers rapidly.

00:16:35.833 --> 00:16:41.866
The period of convalescence for this type of operation is usually ten to fourteen days.

00:16:41.866 --> 00:16:49.046
During the time he is convalescing, the patient also receives intensive medical therapy.

00:16:58.533 --> 00:17:05.233
When discharged, this young man is an ambassador of goodwill for modern medicine in the tropics.

00:17:05.233 --> 00:17:11.473
For back in his tribal village he will report good food, good care, and a speedy recovery.

00:17:15.033 --> 00:17:20.499
As elsewhere, many diseases encountered in the tropics require isolation.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:29.700
The beds in this isolation hospital on the Firestone Plantations are frequently filled with such highly contagious diseases as smallpox and tuberculosis.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:35.100
Of these, smallpox is the more common.

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:38.460
Here are three typical cases.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:46.680
In this case the disease is in an early stage,
as indicated by the cutaneous lesions or skin eruptions.

00:17:55.233 --> 00:17:59.766
This case, a middle-aged woman is more advanced.

00:17:59.766 --> 00:18:07.366
This is a confluent hemorrhagic type of smallpox 
and is characterized by the formation of large pustules over the entire skin surface.

00:18:09.066 --> 00:18:15.866
This case was reported late and terminated fatally.

00:18:25.333 --> 00:18:30.299
The third case, a young boy, is recovering from the disease.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:34.300
The depigmented areas are typical of the recovery stage.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:48.060
In the general hospital are always a variety of diseases, some cosmopolitan, some exclusively tropical.

00:18:55.220 --> 00:19:01.360
Here is a rare case of sarcoma of the clavicle, a cancerous bone tumor.

00:19:01.366 --> 00:19:06.906
Following the failure of surgical and x-ray treatment, the patient died.

00:19:15.966 --> 00:19:23.166
Elephantiasis, a complication of filariasis, is an almost exclusively tropical disease.

00:19:23.166 --> 00:19:29.626
This elephantoid scrotum, weighing 42 pounds, was successfully removed by surgery

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:37.280
and the patient discharged mentally and physically improved.

00:19:47.266 --> 00:19:54.799
Here is a rare clinical example of gynecomastia, 
the development of a female mammary gland in a man.

00:19:54.800 --> 00:20:03.120
This developmental anomaly was corrected surgically with complete success.

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:17.860
A dangerous disease largely confined to tropical Africa is trypanosomiasis, or sleeping sickness.

00:20:17.866 --> 00:20:22.032
Unless treated early, this disease is usually fatal.

00:20:22.033 --> 00:20:26.953
Here, a medical technician punctures a lymph gland of a native worker

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:32.040
whose listless appearance and enlarged cervical glands are symptomatic of sleeping sickness.

00:20:36.833 --> 00:20:46.193
In this particular case, the glandular smear subjected to microscopic examination revealed the trypanosomes which identify this disease.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:56.000
Besides being a public health problem, certain types of trypanosomiasis constitute a major economic drawback

00:20:56.060 --> 00:21:01.460
because they destroy draft animals and other valuable livestock.

00:21:01.466 --> 00:21:05.786
For more routine public health measures, 
some forty dispensaries

00:21:05.786 --> 00:21:09.866
staffed by hospital- trained attendants serve the population of the plantations.

00:21:11.466 --> 00:21:18.132
Evidence of the success of the entire medical program it found in the confidence is has engendered.

00:21:18.133 --> 00:21:27.673
Many who once feared the techniques and paraphernalia of modern medicine are today willing and eager to accept its benefits.

00:21:34.633 --> 00:21:39.899
Much of Liberia's progress in medicine and public health is due to the industrial statesmanship

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:47.560
of Harvey S. Firestone, founder, and Harvey S. Firestone, Junior, now head of the worldwide Firestone organization.

00:21:51.133 --> 00:21:55.853
A gift from that organization enables the American Foundation for Tropical Medicine

00:21:55.860 --> 00:22:01.280
to establish in Liberia a permanent research center for service to tropical medicine generally.

00:22:02.866 --> 00:22:10.132
Mr. Firestone's approval of the model for this Liberian institute was a milestone in tropical medicine.

00:22:10.133 --> 00:22:18.373
World-famous medical authorities and educators have agreed to assist the American Foundation for Tropical Medicine in directing the Liberia institute.

00:22:21.733 --> 00:22:28.833
Continued research, increasing facilities, and the application of the best available skills

00:22:28.833 --> 00:22:35.033
are vitally important to life and progress both in the tropics and out.

00:22:35.033 --> 00:22:44.293
For tropical medicine, whose scope at first glance may appear limited, is actually of basic importance to all peoples and all economies.

00:22:45.833 --> 00:22:52.533
The work already accomplished in Liberia has extended the horizons of general medical knowledge.

00:22:52.533 --> 00:22:59.799
Progress in tropical medicine means progress for business, for science, for humanity.

00:22:59.800 --> 00:23:06.500
The goals are the maximum that can be attained.
Better health, better housing and food,

00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:13.166
improved agriculture and trade, adequate water supplies, and general sanitation.

00:23:13.166 --> 00:23:19.166
Yes, even better transportation and more efficient labor.

00:23:19.166 --> 00:23:25.066
In short, the objectives of tropical medicine are those of all medicine.

00:23:25.066 --> 00:23:27.066
Healthier and happier people.

00:23:27.066 --> 00:23:32.966
Living better with a firmer grasp of the present, and confidence in the future.

00:23:32.966 --> 00:23:38.586
A future which the skills of modern medicine will have made increasingly secure.

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:48.000
[THE END   A Firestone Plantations Company Production]

